From: OpenWrt
Subject: ath10k: ignore unsupported OTP board id with pre-calibration

QCA988x devices using pre-calibration data can report -EOPNOTSUPP when
ath10k tries to query the board id from OTP. The normal firmware probe path
already treats -EOPNOTSUPP as non-fatal and continues with board file loading.

Do the same in the pre-calibration configuration path to avoid aborting or
logging an error for devices whose OTP does not provide a board id.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/core.c
@@ -2285,10 +2285,13 @@ static int ath10k_core_pre_cal_config(st
 	}
 
 	ret = ath10k_core_get_board_id_from_otp(ar);
-	if (ret) {
+	if (ret && ret != -EOPNOTSUPP) {
 		ath10k_err(ar, "failed to get board id: %d\n", ret);
 		return ret;
 	}
+	if (ret == -EOPNOTSUPP)
+		ath10k_dbg(ar, ATH10K_DBG_BOOT,
+			   "boot did not find a pre-calibration board id, continue with board file\n");
 
 	ret = ath10k_download_and_run_otp(ar);
 	if (ret) {
 		ath10k_err(ar, "failed to run otp: %d\n", ret);
